#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""viz_case7_single.py -- ALL-IN-ONE offline renderer for the 7 case-study samples.

Everything is embedded below: per-method (qrad / fastv / divprune) token selections
and scores, plus the 7 images as base64 JPEGs (pre-resized to the render resolution).
Needs only numpy + matplotlib + Pillow. Export THIS ONE FILE and run:

    python3 viz_case7_single.py [outdir]

Writes per sample:  case_<ds>_<idx>_{qrad,fastv,divprune}.pdf   (21 single pages)
and per method:     all_{qrad,fastv,divprune}.pdf               (3 x 7-page pdfs)

Provenance (baked in, computed once on the GPU box with the bench10 code path,
scorer ckpt = ckpt_distill_v8/best.pt, so the drawn selection is exactly the one
that produced the benchmark predictions):
  qrad     distilled CrossAttnScorer student importance, top-20%
  fastv    layer-2 received attention (mean over heads, sum over queries), top-20%
  divprune farthest-point diversity traversal, score = pick order
Colour = RANK of the method's own score within its kept set, on the project's
3-stop ramp blue -> green -> yellow (blue kept per user preference); raw fastv
attention is too skewed to colour directly. Squares = merged-token grid, 28-px
patches in resized space, alpha-blended over the photo (background untouched).
"""
